stion 1 with the corresponding letter numbering>\",\n\"answer_q2\": \"<Respond to the Question 2 with the corresponding letter numbering>\"\n\n    }\n``` \n    \n\n## Scenario\nLiam, a teenager often overlooked by his parents, found pride in keeping a flawless academic record. His parents told him they'd be skipping his awards ceremony for his younger brother's baseball game. With a crushing feeling in his heart, he climbed the stage alone. As he looked into the audience, he saw his parents sitting in the front row, smiling and clapping for him.\n\n## Question 1\nWhat emotion(s) would Liam ultimately feel in this situation?\n\n## Choices for Question 1\nA) Pride\nB) Jealousy\nC) Sadness\nD) Disappointment\nE) Embarrassment\nF) Delight\n\n## Question 2\nWhy would Liam feel these emotions in this situation?\n\n## Choices for Question 2\nA) His parents skipped his younger brother's baseball game to attend his awards ceremony\nB) His flawless academic record has brought him a lot of satisfaction\nC) His parents managed to attend both his ceremony and his brother's baseball game\nD) He was alone on the stage and liked the attention.","options":null,"imageContent":null,"audioContent":null,"videoContent":null,"reminderContext":null,"videoCoverUrl":null,"chips":null,"customMessage":null,"media":null,"mediaTime":null,"interceptContent":null,"contents":[],"imgs":null,"regenerations":0,"seqNum":2,"responseSource":"agent:llm","isSuicide":false,"isSuicideConf":0.010986940930439183,"emotions":[],"relationId":"6af5a09e9aa9dc5a833d8a59","courseProgressId":0,"tsGen":1794482334042,"createTime":"2026-11-12 19:18:54","delFlag":0,"emotionTendency":null,"sourceProductType":null,"sourceProductId":null,"consultantBotId":null,"consultantUserId":null}],"first":true,"last":true},"nonce":"457e46b75d064e50a3baf6ba93d567c9"}